/**
 * @mainpage UART DMA and BLE HCI Toolkit
 *
 * @section overview Overview
 *
 * This project provides a FreeRTOS-backed UART DMA transport, an incremental
 * Bluetooth HCI H4 parser, portable C and Python clients, a continuous BLE-side
 * server, and desktop user interfaces.
 *
 * @section architecture Architecture
 *
 * - @ref uart_dma_core owns the FreeRTOS queues, DMA interrupt integration,
 *   circular receive buffer, CRC validation, and transmit engine.
 * - @ref ble_hci_protocol defines the packed H4 wire layouts and parser API.
 * - @ref app_transport provides portable host serial-port and framed-H4 helpers.
 * - @ref test_transfer defines the deterministic large-transfer test protocol.
 * - The `apps`, `demo`, and `python` directories contain executable front ends.
 *
 * @section framing Wire framing
 *
 * Each transmitted unit consists of an HCI H4 packet followed by a big-endian
 * CRC16-CCITT trailer. Multi-byte Bluetooth fields use little-endian wire order.
 * Packed C structures in ble_hci_wire.h describe each fixed wire header; byte
 * arrays are retained only for variable payloads and incremental byte streams.
 *
 * @section building Building
 *
 * @code{.sh}
 * cmake -S . -B build
 * cmake --build build --parallel
 * ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
 * cmake --build build --target docs
 * @endcode
 */
